  {
   "text": "{\"explanations\":[{\"signal_id\":\"1ee5bad9-99d2-499b-8582-37e22c60500c\",\"explanation\":\"Revenue reached {{fact:32b5f800-7ba4-40ae-a06e-98552fb2dd87}} of plan against a covenant floor of {{fact:97c5f746-53de-4edc-8b8d-533a44d4b33e}}. That leaves headroom of {{fact:ae43e3ef-1fea-4417-960e-f71e423237bb}}, so the covenant level is not being met rather than merely close. The revenue-below-plan and falling-headroom signals describe the same shortfall.\"},{\"signal_id\":\"776afc92-b41f-4c74-8e53-d5af07f14146\",\"explanation\":\"Revenue came in at {{fact:4bf4d2f4-2224-4f95-9d8b-41d59d1dd898}} of plan. For a SaaS borrower, that points to weaker bookings, churn or delayed renewals. This is the operating cause behind the revenue covenant shortfall, and it may also explain the steady erosion in cash headroom.\"},{\"signal_id\":\"6eb79603-81fc-4ff1-a0fd-3a9e4025d7e0\",\"explanation\":\"Revenue covenant headroom has slid each month: from {{fact:42050e4a-ce3c-4af0-ba42-72b6a00e7406}} in August, to {{fact:7811a1dd-1c93-4785-9b8d-f5db44b8c429}} in September, to {{fact:ae43e3ef-1fea-4417-960e-f71e423237bb}} in October. The shortfall began in September and deepened in October, so it is a worsening trend rather than a one-month miss.\"},{\"signal_id\":\"42211345-4a14-4cea-bbf2-9ca80c14f6fb\",\"explanation\":\"Unrestricted cash of {{fact:29cd8d28-78a3-4c0b-a29d-b33eca788e0c}} remains comfortably above the {{fact:69ddefe1-73f7-4ffa-9ce8-bbaef95ad183}} minimum. However, headroom has declined steadily, from {{fact:49054f80-7d19-4d2e-a0c2-66cc7628c4cd}} to {{fact:8ce31a07-18b0-4706-ae13-cb74dd1b2656}} to {{fact:8d80b4d7-54c2-4f69-a386-50366ce31c62}}. Taken together with the revenue shortfall, this suggests cash burn is drawing down the liquidity cushion.\"}],\"ranking\":[\"1ee5bad9-99d2-499b-8582-37e22c60500c\",\"776afc92-b41f-4c74-8e53-d5af07f14146\",\"6eb79603-81fc-4ff1-a0fd-3a9e4025d7e0\",\"42211345-4a14-4cea-bbf2-9ca80c14f6fb\"]}",
   "type": "text"
  }
